---
// How the parts fit together's diagram: Thermite's parts as nested boxes, in plain HTML, so
// it wraps on a phone, follows the site's light and dark themes and stays real text. The
// numbers in it match the steps of a run that the page lists under it.
---

<figure class="hiw not-content" aria-labelledby="hiw-caption">
  <div class="top">
    <div class="box you">
      <p class="name">You</p>
      <p>and your scripts and agents, through the dashboard, the REST API, MCP or the <code>thermite</code> command line.</p>
      <span class="n" title="Step 1">1</span>
    </div>
    <div class="link across"><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>watch and steer</span></div>
    <div class="box control">
      <p class="name">Control <span class="role">one central service</span></p>
      <p class="note">It shows what the rigs report and signs what you decide. It measures nothing and decides no verdict.</p>
      <div class="parts four">
        <div class="part"><b>Dashboard</b><span>every campaign, run and rig; <b>Live</b> and <b>Needs you</b></span></div>
        <div class="part"><b>REST API, MCP, CLI</b><span>the same actions for scripts and agents</span></div>
        <div class="part"><b>Store</b><span>campaigns, kits, reports and signed commands, with keys sealed</span></div>
        <div class="part"><b>Knowledge base</b><span>a folder for each campaign, which later runs read</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="link down wide">
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span><b>The rig dials out:</b> reports and live lines go up, signed commands come down. Control never connects into a rig.</span>
    <span class="n" title="Step 8">8</span>
  </div>

  <div class="box rig">
    <p class="name">A rig <span class="role">one of many: on your machine, a Kubernetes cluster or a RunPod pod</span></p>
    <p class="note">Two containers, split by what each is trusted with. A rig works on one run at a time.</p>

    <div class="box container supervisor">
      <p class="name">Supervisor <span class="role">the rig's link to the outside</span></p>
      <p class="note">It holds the rig's git and control credentials, and runs no code that an agent wrote.</p>
      <div class="parts sup">
        <div class="part"><b>Relay</b><span>carries reports up and commands down; it can forge neither</span><span class="n" title="Step 2">2</span></div>
        <div class="part"><b>Git</b><span>fetches the project, kit and models a command names; pushes the results</span></div>
        <div class="group">
          <p class="gname">The advisors <span class="role">they steer; they never judge</span></p>
          <div class="parts three">
            <div class="part"><b>Teachers</b><span>read the results and the champion's code; add ideas to the queue and rules for the planner</span><span class="n" title="Step 7">7</span></div>
            <div class="part"><b>Auditor</b><span>checks a surprising win before it is kept</span><span class="n" title="Step 6">6</span></div>
            <div class="part"><b>Review panel</b><span>scores the goals that code can't measure, and finds when a research run's questions are answered</span><span class="n" title="Step 7">7</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="link down"><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>commands in, signed events out</span></div>

    <div class="bottom">
      <div class="box container harness">
        <p class="name">Harness <span class="role">where the research happens</span></p>
        <p class="note">It runs code that agents wrote, so it reaches only its model and the internet.</p>
        <div class="flow">
          <div class="part"><b>Experiment queue and planner</b><span>one list of what to try; each round, the planner gives each lane its next experiment, never the same one to two lanes</span><span class="n" title="Step 3">3</span></div>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="part lanes">
            <b>Lanes</b>
            <span class="worker">worker · lane 1</span>
            <span class="worker">worker · lane 2</span>
            <span class="worker more">…</span>
            <span>each trial is a fresh agent session in its own copy of the code, and submits one change</span>
            <span class="n" title="Step 4">4</span>
          </div>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="part judge"><b>Judge</b><span>builds the change, times it against the champion or checks each goal, and confirms a win on fresh runs and hidden cases</span><span class="n" title="Step 5">5</span></div>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="part"><b>Champion</b><span>the best code so far, which the next trials build on</span><span class="n" title="Step 6">6</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="parts two base">
          <div class="part"><b>Ledger</b><span>the rig's own database: every experiment, attempt, measurement, verdict and champion</span><span class="n" title="Step 8">8</span></div>
          <div class="part"><b>Broker</b><span>starts every process as its own user, so no agent can read or change the judge</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="link across"><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>timed runs</span></div>
      <div class="box target">
        <p class="name">Target</p>
        <p>The CPU or the GPUs the work is measured on, through a target driver. The judge holds the clock; nothing a change prints is its score.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="outside">
    <div class="box ext"><b>Model providers</b><span>the agents' and the advisors' models: API keys, Claude or ChatGPT subscriptions, or a server of your own</span></div>
    <div class="box ext"><b>Git</b><span>your project, its kits and your results repository</span></div>
  </div>

  <figcaption id="hiw-caption">
    Thermite's parts: you steer through control; each rig's supervisor links it to control and to git and runs its advisors; its harness runs the planner, the workers in their lanes and the judge, which measures every change on the target. The numbers are the steps of a run, below.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .hiw {
    --hiw-line: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    --hiw-soft: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    --hiw-card: var(--sl-color-bg);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--sl-color-text);
  }
  .hiw p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hiw code {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .box {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--hiw-line);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    background: var(--hiw-card);
  }
  .name {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .role {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    margin-inline-start: 0.375rem;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem !important;
  }
  .top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 1fr) auto 3.5fr;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .you {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .control {
    border: 2px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  .rig {
    border: 2px dashed var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    background: transparent;
  }
  .container {
    background: var(--hiw-soft);
  }
  .supervisor {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .parts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .parts.four {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  }
  .parts.three {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
  .parts.two {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }
  .parts.sup {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 3fr;
  }
  .part {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hiw-line);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.625rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--hiw-card);
  }
  .part > b {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .part > span:not(.n):not(.worker) {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .group {
    border: 1px solid var(--hiw-line);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
  }
  .gname {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin: 0 0 0.375rem 0.25rem !important;
  }
  .bottom {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4fr auto 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr auto 1.2fr auto 1.2fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .flow > .arrow {
    align-self: center;
  }
  .judge {
    border: 2px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  .worker {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--hiw-line);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .worker.more {
    border: none;
    padding: 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .target {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    background: var(--hiw-soft);
  }
  .target > p:not(.name) {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .outside {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .ext {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    border-style: dotted;
  }
  .ext > b {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .ext > span {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .link.across {
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 7rem;
  }
  .link.down {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .link.wide {
    padding: 0.625rem 2.5rem;
  }
  .arrow::before {
    content: "→";
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  .link.down .arrow::before {
    content: "⇅";
  }
  .link.across .arrow::before {
    content: "⇄";
  }
  .n {
    position: absolute;
    top: -0.625rem;
    right: -0.5rem;
    min-width: 1.375rem;
    height: 1.375rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent);
    color: var(--sl-color-black);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.375rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .link .n {
    position: static;
    flex: none;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  /* On a narrow screen every row stacks, and the arrows point down. */
  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .top,
    .bottom,
    .flow,
    .parts.four,
    .parts.three,
    .parts.sup,
    .parts.two,
    .outside {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .link.across {
      flex-direction: row;
      max-width: none;
      padding: 0.25rem 0;
    }
    .link.wide {
      padding: 0.5rem 0;
    }
    .arrow::before,
    .link.across .arrow::before {
      content: "↓";
    }
    .link.down .arrow::before {
      content: "⇅";
    }
    .flow > .arrow {
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }
</style>
